  "title": "Kourovka Notebook Problem 21.111",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $S$ be a finite simple nonabelian group that is not isomorphic to any group ${}^2B_2(q)$. A nonidentity automorphism $x$ of $S$ is called a $\\tau$-automorphism if every two conjugates of $x$ in $\\langle x,\\operatorname{Inn}(S)\\rangle$ generate a subgroup of order not divisible by 3. If $S$ admits a $\\tau$-automorphism, we call $S$ a $\\tau$-group.\n\n(a) List all $\\tau$-groups up to isomorphism.\n\n(b) Do $\\tau$-automorphisms of odd order exist?",
    "sha256": "6c216d4794da01771e77d2e94b85013933d4b6c940cf462cdb58ce8f74eeac53",
